      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The influence of PGE1, iloprost and a combination of both on high energy phosphate levels in isolated rat hearts reperfused 1 h following 20 min of global ischemia was investigated employing 31P-NMR-spectroscopy. Whereas PGE1 induced a slight reduction in the decline of the creatine phosphate/inorganic phosphate. ATP/inorganic phosphate ratio and NMR-energetic index during ischemia, iloprost application was followed predominantly by a temporary but marked improvement of the creatine phosphate/inorganic phosphate ratio during the early period of reperfusion. The best results in preservation of high energy phosphates were achieved after simultaneous application of PGE1 and iloprost. It is presumed that the accelerated normalization of the heart function observed immediately after ischemia in the eicosanoid treated hearts is related to the more rapid recovery of intracardial high energy phosphate level."},
